\textbf{Real-world protocol.} The real-world setup (\cref{fig:env}) uses a Franka Emika Panda arm and more than 2k demonstrations over six skills. We test three kinds of tasks with 20 trials each: seen tasks, grasping of unseen objects which stresses semantic generalization, and precise operations such as cable routing and small-object grasping which stress spatial detail.

\textbf{Real world.} In \cref{fig:real}, LLM-backbone methods outperform RT-1 and Diffusion Policy on seen tasks, with UP-VLA competitive or best. On unseen-object grasping UP-VLA-RT-2 outperforms UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu, and UP-VLA is best overall, indicating semantic gains from MMU and its alignment with actions. On precision tasks UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu outperforms UP-VLA-RT-2 and UP-VLA is best, highlighting the benefit of future prediction for spatial detail.

